    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2bf8f46f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: officer_down_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two police officers in motion, with one appearing to be running or falling, while the text 'officer down' is overlaid. This visual is commonly used as a meme to humorously or sarcastically imply that a situation has gone awry, often in a context where someone is being 'taken down' or 'outsmarted'. The intent is not to target any specific group based on protected characteristics, but rather to use the trope of 'officer down' for comedic effect. However, the phrase 'officer down' is associated with real-life emergency situations involving police officers being injured or killed, which can be harmful if used irresponsibly or in contexts that trivialize real tragedies. The meme's intent is primarily humorous or satirical, but its potential to cause harm arises from the real-world gravity of the phrase, which may be seen as insensitive or disrespectful when used inappropriately.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_feff1c10"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
